51271.body:
Adds PerfTools/Perfetto, an EDM service (PerfettoTraceService) that records an in-process Perfetto (https://perfetto.dev) trace (.pftrace) of a cmsRun job,  openable by drag-and-drop at https://perfetto.web.cern.ch , entirely client-side, together with a small dependency-free monitor hook in HeterogeneousCore/AlpakaInterface that the Alpaka caching allocator uses to report device-memory traffic.
What it records:
 

-  module / acquire / EventSetup / source / cleanup slices on a per-(stream, thread) lane under each `edm::stream`, so independent modules running concurrently within a stream, and an ExternalWork module's `acquire()`/`produce()` running on different threads  nest correctly without overlapping or mis-paired slices;
-  a global Throughput (events/s) counter plus per-stream run/lumi/event counters;
-  (optional, traceAllocations) Alpaka caching-allocator transactions: each alloc/free attributed to the module that triggered it, plus per-device live/cached/requested device-memory counters;
-  (optional, traceGpuKernels) CUDA kernel activity via CUPTI: real device-side start/end, registers per thread, static and dynamic shared memory, per-thread and total local memory, an estimated occupancy, and the CUPTI correlation id linking each kernel back to the host module that launched it;
-  (optional, tracePower) CPU (RAPL) and GPU (NVML) power as counter tracks, at a configurable sampling period;
-  `CMS_PERFETTO_FUNC()/CMS_PERFETTO_SCOPE()` macros for optional intra-module instrumentation, and a traceModules filter for focused, low-overhead runs.

Everything beyond the per-stream slices and counters is opt-in and off by default: with the optional features disabled the per-allocation cost is a single relaxed atomic load, and disabled trace categories cost only a predicated load.

Usage: `cmsDriver.py  --customise PerfTools/Perfetto/customisePerfetto.customise`, or add the service directly; see `PerfTools/Perfetto/README.md`

@rovere @makortel @fwyzard

52479.body:
This PR makes the TICLGeom geometry one EventSetup product with a simple interface for host code and for Alpaka kernels.

**One product.** `TICLGeomSoA` now has five blocks: `common`, `silicon`, `scint`, `lookup` and `layers`. `TICLGeomESProducer` fills all five. The separate products `TICLGeomLookupHost` and `TICLGeomLayersHost`, their device twins, their ES producers and their HLT cfis are removed. A consumer now needs one ES token instead of three. The `lookup` block has 0 rows for a product without HGCAL cells, so the `ECAL` and `HCAL` products do not carry the 8 MB lookup table.

**Device interface.** The geometry functions are methods of the SoA `ConstView` (`SOA_CONST_VIEW_METHODS` of `GENERATE_SOA_BLOCKS`). All methods are host and device functions:

```cpp
// producer
device::ESGetToken<TICLGeomDevice, CaloGeometryRecord> ticlGeomToken_;
const TICLGeomSoAConstView geom = iSetup.getData(ticlGeomToken_).const_view();
// pass geom to the kernel by value

// kernel
const auto cell = geom.cell(rawDetId);  // one lookup
if (cell.valid()) {
  const auto pos = cell.position();
  const int layer = cell.layerWithOffset();
  if (cell.isSilicon()) {
    const float thickness = cell.thickness();
  }
}
```

- `geom.cell(rawDetId)` finds the row with the lookup block (one table read and a binary search over one wafer or ring) for HGCAL detids, and with a binary search over all cells for other detids. `geom.cellAt(i)` gives the cell at row `i`.
- `ticlgeom::Cell` has short getters: position, eta, phi, pt, zside, layer, type, sensor group, cassette, mask, the silicon getters and the scintillator getters. A getter of an invalid cell, or of a cell of the other type, returns a documented default value.
- The view also has `layerZ`, `noseLayerZ`, `barrelLayerPosition` and the geometry-wide getters (`lastLayerEE`, `numberOfLayers`, ...).
- A `Cell` points to its view and is valid only while that view exists. `cell` and `cellAt` are deleted for a temporary view, so `const_view().cell(id)` does not compile.

**Host interface.** `ticlgeom::Tools::setGeometry` takes the one product. All `Tools` getters keep their names and results. The getters that read a column use `ticlgeom::Cell`, so host and device share one implementation of them; the getters that decode the detid bits (`zside`, `getLayer`, `getWafer`, `getCell`, `isSilicon`, ...) are unchanged. `Tools::geom()` returns the `ConstView`.

**Removed functions.** No code in master uses them: `Tools::commonView`, `siliconView`, `scintView`, `lookupView` and `layersView`, the index helpers `Tools::siliconLocal` and `scintLocal`, and the free functions `ticlgeom::etaFromVertex`, `ticlgeom::pt` and `ticlgeom::isOnlySilicon`.

**Consumers.** About 40 C++ files drop the lookup and layers ES tokens. The offline `TICLGeom_cff` and `hgcalLocalReco_cff` and the `HLT_75e33`, `HLT_75e33_timing` and `HLT_NGTScouting` menus no longer load the removed producers. In `BarrelLayerClusterProducer` and `HGCalLayerClusterProducer`, `std::unique_ptr<...>(new ...)` becomes `std::make_unique`, as code-checks requires.

**Tests.** `RecoTICL/Geometry/test/TICLGeomAnalyzer_cfg.py` is now the unit test `testTICLGeomClosure`. It runs on the default, `ECAL`, `HCAL` and `withBarrel` products.
- `TICLGeomDeviceTest` calls every `ConstView` and `Cell` getter on the device for every cell and every layer row, and compares the results with `ticlgeom::Tools` on the host. It runs on the default, `ECAL` and `withBarrel` products. It also checks the default values for detids that the collection does not hold (also an absent cell inside a filled wafer and inside a filled scintillator ring), for `cellAt` outside the rows and for an out-of-range layer.
- `TICLGeomAnalyzer` checks every column, both lookups and the `Tools` getters against `hgcal::RecHitTools`. A `static_assert` checks that a temporary view cannot give a `Cell`.

52500.body:
#### PR description:

This PR fixes three bugs in the seeds that `LSTOutputConverter` makes for mkFit (HLT default menu; offline `highPtTripletStep` in the LST workflows).

- **pT3/pT5 hit order.** A pixel-track OT hit and an LST hit on overlapping modules of one layer were sorted by the module's `rSpan().first` (`|zSpan().first|` in the endcap), which can tie or invert in the tilted barrel. `makeSeed` then failed for 8-9% of the pT3/pT5 objects in the HLT, and their seeds fell back to the pixel seed without LST's OT hits. Hits are now sorted by layer, then by the distance of the sensor plane from the origin along the plane normal (the plane's radius in the flat barrel, its |z| in the endcap).
- **T4 helix start.** It could use the two hits of one module. Then 1.5-3% of the T4 objects gave no seed, and another 15-17% got a seed with a badly measured curvature, part of them below the 0.8 GeV LST cut (plots below). T5 and T4 now share one rule: the helix starts from two hits on different modules, neither on a PS strip sensor.
- **Empty seed.** A failed inner-tracker-only pLS seed read `seeds[0]` from an empty vector; the input pixel seed is now kept.

Duplicate rate of the LST seeds for mkFit in the HLT (ttbar, QCD). The seeds below 0.5 GeV go from about one per event on master to 0.01-0.02.

<img src="https://gniendorf.github.io/lst-plots-2/internal-prs/lst-converter-seed-fixes/desc/seed_duplrate_pt_ttbar.png" width="350"> <img src="https://gniendorf.github.io/lst-plots-2/internal-prs/lst-converter-seed-fixes/desc/seed_duplrate_pt_qcd.png" width="350">

#### PR validation:

CMSSW_20_1_X_2026-11-09-1100 with only this PR. Master  this PR, CPU, PU200, the same events (ttbar / QCD):
- HLT, 5000 + 5000 events, hltGeneralTracks:
  - prompt efficiency (vxy < 2.5 cm): 89.20%  89.20% / 88.86%  88.87%, unchanged;
  - efficiency at vxy 32-60 cm: 51.2%  53.3% / 41.6%  43.4%;
  - fake rate: 1.07%  1.05% / 1.27%  1.24%;
  - duplicate rate: 1.00%  1.01% / 0.98%  1.00%;
  - +0.10 hits per track.

  Plots: [ttbar](https://gniendorf.github.io/lst-plots-2/internal-prs/lst-converter-seed-fixes/hlt_ttbar/plots_hlt.html), [QCD](https://gniendorf.github.io/lst-plots-2/internal-prs/lst-converter-seed-fixes/hlt_qcd/plots_hlt.html)
- Offline 34634.711, 2000 + 2000 events, generalTracks (only the T4 fix acts offline: offline pixel seeds have no OT hits):
  - efficiency: 88.66%  88.67% / 86.36%  86.34%;
  - efficiency at 32-63 cm production radius: 39.6%  40.1% / 29.8%  30.8%;
  - fake rate: 7.63%  7.60% / 7.68%  7.65%;
  - duplicate rate: 0.90%  0.91% / 0.90%  0.91%.

  Plots: [ttbar](https://gniendorf.github.io/lst-plots-2/internal-prs/lst-converter-seed-fixes/off01_ttbar/index.html), [QCD](https://gniendorf.github.io/lst-plots-2/internal-prs/lst-converter-seed-fixes/off01_qcd/index.html); all iterations (34634.714), 500 + 500 events: [ttbar](https://gniendorf.github.io/lst-plots-2/internal-prs/lst-converter-seed-fixes/offall_ttbar/index.html), [QCD](https://gniendorf.github.io/lst-plots-2/internal-prs/lst-converter-seed-fixes/offall_qcd/index.html)
- HLT timing, CPU menu, ttbar, thread time per event (8 jobs  16 threads): converter 55.1  44.9 ms, mkFit 62.7  57.6 ms, whole job 0.9%.

